11.0.0, fourteenth upload — your pulse from the camera, the Field in Metal, a seventh synth engine, the Echoel look and number pad, a safer take

What is new since 10017 (10018 carried only the DDSP engine). Each line is code that the Echoel
Studio run builds and, where a test target reaches it, tests; nothing here is device-verified yet.
- Body Source in the Song menu: Off, Heart Rate Strap or Camera, one at a time. Camera measures
  the pulse from a fingertip on the rear lens with the light on; frames are reduced to brightness
  numbers on the device and discarded. A cue line under the transport says what to do.
- The Field is drawn by Metal at 60 frames per second: colour from the key, rings from the beat,
  a bloom from the heartbeat, every flash held under three per second. It floats as a small
  window and opens to full screen.
- Engine = DDSP, a seventh synth engine: a bank of harmonics plus filtered noise, Character moves
  the timbre.
- A take ends cleanly before any audio graph rebuild and is placed with the tempo map it began
  under; position arithmetic saturates instead of crashing on extreme songs; an export longer
  than a WAV file can hold is refused at once instead of failing late.
- The earlier instrument's look: black ground, one green accent, the Atkinson Hyperlegible
  face, and Echoel's own number pad — tap a value on the Sound page, an effect or the mixer level
  to type it exactly (− and + set the sign where the range allows).
- Every save keeps the song one save back; a damaged song opens from that copy and says so.
- If playback stops rendering while playing, the audio graph rebuilds itself. After two launch
  crashes in a row, the next launch starts safe (no floating Field, other makers' plug-ins only
  after you confirm).

Previous: 11.0.0 (10018), thirteenth upload — the DDSP engine alone. 10017/10015, twelfth —
six synth engines, tone system and concert pitch in the Key menu, the body moves a send. 10014 —
HRV and coherence as sources. 10013 — your pulse moves the mix. 10012 — heart rate strap.
Before that: 10011 down to 10004 (the first Echoel Studio build).
group.com.echoelmusic (the import of earlier songs) is still not requested (F17).

Bump this file on a commit whose "Echoel Studio" run is green to upload a build
(.github/workflows/studio-testflight.yml). Build number = 10000 + the workflow's run number.
The version is MARKETING_VERSION in EchoelStudio/project.yml.
This file is a test list for the device, not a source for claims (ContentPipeline/CLAIMS.md).

Five things to try on the device (FOUNDER_INBOX rule 1: five per build; answer each yes or no):
1. Song menu, Body Source = Camera: iOS asks for the camera once, the light comes on and stays on;
   fingertip on the lens, and within about 20 seconds a pulse appears beside Record.
2. Lift the finger: the pulse disappears within about 5 seconds; Body Source = Off turns the light
   and the camera indicator off. Menus stay usable the whole time.
3. The Field window: colour, rings and bloom move with the song and the pulse, no flicker at a
   fast tempo, and full screen opens and closes without a stuck screen.
4. Sound page, Engine = DDSP: hold a chord and turn Character; the timbre changes without a click
   and no note sticks.
5. Sound page, tap Attack: Echoel's number pad opens with "ms" and − disabled; type 250 and OK,
   and the value reads 250 ms. Record a short take afterwards: it lands where it was played.
